      "$description": "The numbered aliases are not appearance tokens. They exist for the vendored PrimeVue sheet, which reads them as a fixed Tailwind style ladder where 0 is the lightest surface and 950 the darkest, and which already chooses between light and dark with its own dark: variant. A token that flips underneath that variant flips twice, and two flips cancel: the light branch asked for white and got the darkest neutral, which is why every preset panel painted black in the light appearance. Both appearances therefore reference one ladder. The semantic names above are the ones that carry the appearance, and nothing in our own markup reads a numbered alias any more.",
