    "syntax": {
      "$description": "The editor's syntax colours. Tier 2 under foundations/colour.md: they are decorative, they carry no status, and no intent in the system means what any of them mean, so they take their own namespace with their own value per appearance rather than aliasing a ramp. The dark values are the ones the product already shipped and nineteen of the twenty-two are preserved byte for byte. Three were below the 4.5 text floor against the page and were lifted in lightness at fixed hue and chroma, which is the smallest move that clears the gate: punctuation from 3.78 to 4.56, comment from 3.77 to 4.52 and js-keyword from 4.02 to 4.52. The light values are derived the way the row highlights are, by walking lightness in the light ramp's own direction until the same floor is met, with chroma clamped into gamut at each step. The js- names are a second palette rather than a duplicate of the first: the JavaScript editor ships a Tomorrow Night set where the rest of the product ships a VS Code Dark+ derivative, and collapsing the two would repaint both.",
